{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-401f9991-bfb7-4e11-affb-77b1b44f75f5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-838b41f81ea7e524","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-1dm70if8/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers per-project idle resource reporting in the RHOAI web\nconsole so cluster administrators can see which resources are sitting idle\nand reclaim capacity with confidence. It adds two report views: an\nidle-workbench report showing each workbench's last activity, owner, and\nreserved resources, and a stale pipeline-run report showing completed runs\nolder than a configurable age with their retained artifacts. Both reports\nare read-only surfaces over data that already exists in the platform —\nnotebook-controller activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata —\nso this epic changes only the web console; the data-source components keep\nworking unchanged. Administrators can also export either report as CSV.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a per-project idle-workbench report view to the web console showing,\n  per workbench: last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's\n  activity tracking), owner, and reserved resources.\n- Add a per-project stale pipeline-run report view to the console showing\n  completed pipeline runs older than a configurable age threshold, with\n  their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Make the stale-run age threshold configurable.\n- Add CSV export of either report, containing the columns the report\n  displays.\n- Validation of the passive data sources: confirm the idle-workbench report\n  matches notebook-controller activity data, and the stale-run report\n  matches Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata, without changes to either\n  data-source component.\n- No automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources, and no\n  cost/chargeback calculations (out of scope per the strategy).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project containing workbenches with differing recent activity,\n  when an administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then every\n  workbench in the project is listed with its last-activity timestamp,\n  owner, and reserved resources, and the values match the notebook\n  controller's activity tracking.\n- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs of differing ages with\n  retained artifacts, when an administrator opens the stale pipeline-run\n  report with a configured age threshold, then exactly the completed runs\n  older than that threshold are listed with their completion age and\n  retained artifacts, and the values match Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Given the stale pipeline-run report, when an administrator changes the age\n  threshold configuration, then the report reflects the new threshold\n  without code changes.\n- Given either report, when an administrator triggers CSV export, then a CSV\n  file is produced containing the report's displayed rows and columns.\n- The notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines components require no code\n  changes for either report to function (verified against a running\n  platform).\n- Measured by: report correctness verified against the underlying\n  notebook-controller activity data and Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata in a\n  test project.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n  reserved resources) sourced from notebook-controller activity tracking —\n  covered by the idle-workbench report scope above.\n- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n  run metadata — covered by the stale-run report scope above.\n- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — bundled into this epic\n  because it exports the same report data and renders on the same report\n  surfaces this epic builds; a separate epic would build the same surfaces\n  twice or force a second pass over them.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The strategy asserts the notebook-controller last-activity data exists\n  and only needs surfacing. If the activity timestamps are not readable\n  through an interface the console can consume, a follow-up change in the\n  notebook controller (Notebooks component, Workbenches team) may be\n  required — escalate if that exposure work turns out to be non-trivial.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29312,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d306432b1cb6747","agent_id":"a3057503c794963b7","session_id":"14fa2f4a-f3d4-41e5-9c0e-f94b0cf4c56f","uuid":"075be2f7-cbcd-499d-815b-81f4cbe82360","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:12:52.110Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
