{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b166ced9-f925-4c2b-9baa-3d916716a975","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93966253a01f40bf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-1dm70if8/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E002.md","content":"# Document the idle/stale resource reports and safe reclamation steps\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers user documentation for the idle resource reporting\ncapability in the RHOAI web console. It explains the two reports — the\nper-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved\nresources) and the stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\nconfigurable age with retained artifacts) — how to read and configure them,\nhow to export them as CSV, and the safe steps administrators can take to\nreclaim capacity based on what the reports show. It is written against the\nimplemented reports after the console work is complete.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline:\n\n- A documentation topic introducing idle resource reporting: what problem\n  it solves for cluster administrators and where the reports live in the\n  web console.\n- A topic explaining the idle-workbench report: what each column (last\n  activity, owner, reserved resources) means, where the data comes from\n  (notebook-controller activity tracking), and its limitations.\n- A topic explaining the stale pipeline-run report: what \"stale\" means, how\n  to configure the age threshold, what retained artifacts are, and where\n  the data comes from (Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata).\n- A topic covering CSV export of either report.\n- A topic on safe reclamation steps: how administrators can act on the\n  reports to reclaim capacity with confidence, including appropriate\n  cautions (e.g., checking with a workbench owner before acting, retaining\n  artifacts that matter). Automated reclamation is out of scope for the\n  feature and