pelines | `Data Science Pipelines` | Passive (no code changes; data source) | RHOAI Pipelines |\n43\t\n44\tBoth passive components are corroborated by architecture context: the\n45\tnotebook controller tracks last activity per kernel\n46\t(`notebooks.md`), and Kubeflow Pipelines retains run completion metadata\n47\texposed via the KFP v2 REST API with pipeline runs already surfaced in the\n48\tDashboard (`data-science-pipelines.md`). Per the passive-component rule,\n49\tvalidation of both data sources becomes acceptance criteria on the Dashboard\n50\timplementation epic (the nearest active component). The different-team\n51\tvalidation exception does not fire: the RHOAI Dashboard team consumes and\n52\tvalidates both data sources as part of building the reports, and the strategy\n53\tstates no code changes in either passive component. All three components\n54\texist in the platform (architecture context files present), so no onboarding\n55\tchain is needed; the Dashboard is already Konflux-onboarded\n56\t(`dashboard.md`).\n57\t\n58\t## Investigation Epics (Step 3)\n59\t\n60\tThe strategy's open questions table is explicitly \"None\"; there are no risks,\n61\tassumptions, pending reviews, or conditional ADRs. No Investigation epics.\n62\t\n63\tOne residual detail was evaluated and classified as an implementation\n64\tdetail, not a genuine unknown: the exact interface through which the console\n65\treads notebook-controller last-activity timestamps (the culler tracks them\n66\tvia Jupyter server API probes per `notebooks.md`, and the Dashboard consumes\n67\tthe Kubernetes API per `dashboard.md`). The strategy asserts the data exists\n68\tand frames the work as surfacing it; discovering the concrete API surface is\n69\tresolved when the team starts the work. It is captured as an acceptance\n70\tcriterion and a health warning below, not an Investigation epic.\n71\t\n72\t## Epic List\n73\t\n74\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n75\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n76\t| RHA