{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98c180a9aa9d3a38","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers per-project idle resource reporting in the RHOAI web\n34\tconsole so cluster administrators can see which resources are sitting idle\n35\tand reclaim capacity with confidence. It adds two report views: an\n36\tidle-workbench report showing each workbench's last activity, owner, and\n37\treserved resources, and a stale pipeline-run report showing completed runs\n38\tolder than a configurable age with their retained artifacts. Both reports\n39\tare read-only surfaces over data that already exists in the platform —\n40\tnotebook-controller activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata —\n41\tso this epic changes only the web console; the data-source components keep\n42\tworking unchanged. Administrators can also export either report as CSV.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Add a per-project idle-workbench report view to the web console showing,\n47\t  per workbench: last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's\n48\t  activity tracking), owner, and reserved resources.\n49\t- Add a per-project stale pipeline-run report view to the console showing\n50\t  completed pipeline runs older than a configurable age threshold, with\n51\t  their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n52\t- Make the stale-run age threshold configurable.\n53\t- Add CSV export of either report, containing the columns the report\n54\t  displays.\n55\t- Validation of the passive data sources: confirm the idle-workbench report\n56\t  matches notebook-controller activity data, and the stale-run report\n57\t  matches Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata, without changes to either\n58\t  data-source component.\n59\t- No automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources, and no\n60\t  cost/chargeback calculations (out of scope per the strategy).\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Given a project containing workbenches with differing recent activity,\n65\t  when an administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then every\n66\t  workbench in the project is listed with its last-activity timestamp,\n67\t  owner, and reserved resources, and the values match the notebook\n68\t  controller's activity tracking.\n69\t- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs of differing ages with\n70\t  retained artifacts, when an administrator opens the stale pipeline-run\n71\t  report with a configured age threshold, then exactly the completed runs\n72\t  older than that threshold are listed with their completion age and\n73\t  retained artifacts, and the values match Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n74\t- Given the stale pipeline-run report, when an administrator changes the age\n75\t  threshold configuration, then the report reflects the new threshold\n76\t  without code changes.\n77\t- Given either report, when an administrator triggers CSV export, then a CSV\n78\t  file is produced containing the report's displayed rows and columns.\n79\t- The notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines components require no code\n80\t  changes for either report to function (verified against a running\n81\t  platform).\n82\t- Measured by: report correctness verified against the underlying\n83\t  notebook-controller activity data and Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata in a\n84\t  test project.\n85\t\n86\t## HLR Traceability\n87\t\n88\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n89\t  reserved resources) sourced from notebook-controller activity tracking —\n90\t  covered by the idle-workbench report scope above.\n91\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n92\t  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n93\t  run metadata — covered by the stale-run report scope above.\n94\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — bundled into this epic\n95\t  because it exports the same report data and renders on the same report\n96\t  surfaces this epic builds; a separate epic would build the same surfaces\n97\t  twice or force a second pass over them.\n98\t\n99\t## Risks / Notes\n100\t\n101\t- The strategy asserts the notebook-controller last-activity data exists\n102\t  and only needs surfacing. If the activity timestamps are not readable\n103\t  through an interface the console can consume, a follow-up change in the\n104\t  notebook controller (Notebooks component, Workbenches team) may be\n105\t  required — escalate if that exposure work turns out to be non-trivial.\n106\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-945aaabf66655e09","agent_id":"a8655c8f05f6a5029","session_id":"14fa2f4a-f3d4-41e5-9c0e-f94b0cf4c56f","uuid":"d5055cbb-e3f6-4b85-bd90-ca72b7479ffa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:18:43.871Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98c180a9aa9d3a38","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
