{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8adf36c08a82f201","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E002\n3\ttitle: Document the idle/stale resource reports and safe reclamation steps\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: Documentation\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Document the idle/stale resource reports and safe reclamation steps\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers user documentation for the idle resource reporting\n35\tcapability in the RHOAI web console. It explains the two reports — the\n36\tper-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved\n37\tresources) and the stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n38\tconfigurable age with retained artifacts) — how to read and configure them,\n39\thow to export them as CSV, and the safe steps administrators can take to\n40\treclaim capacity based on what the reports show. It is written against the\n41\timplemented reports after the console work is complete.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\tContent outline:\n46\t\n47\t- A documentation topic introducing idle resource reporting: what problem\n48\t  it solves for cluster administrators and where the reports live in the\n49\t  web console.\n50\t- A topic explaining the idle-workbench report: what each column (last\n51\t  activity, owner, reserved resources) means, where the data comes from\n52\t  (notebook-controller activity tracking), and its limitations.\n53\t- A topic explaining the stale pipeline-run report: what \"stale\" means, how\n54\t  to configure the age threshold, what retained artifacts are, and where\n55\t  the data comes from (Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata).\n56\t- A topic covering CSV export of either report.\n57\t- A topic on safe reclamation steps: how administrators can act on the\n58\t  reports to reclaim capacity with confidence, including appropriate\n59\t  cautions (e.g., checking with a workbench owner before acting, retaining\n60\t  artifacts that matter). Automated reclamation is out of scope for the\n61\t  feature and must not be documented as available.\n62\t- Screenshots of the report views and export flow as part of the topics.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- Published documentation explains both reports, the meaning of each\n67\t  reported field, the configurable stale-run age threshold, and CSV export.\n68\t- Published documentation describes safe reclamation steps an administrator\n69\t  can take based on the reports, and does not describe automated\n70\t  reclamation/deletion or cost/chargeback capabilities (out of scope per the\n71\t  strategy).\n72\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented reports\n73\t  in the web console and matches the shipped behavior (columns, thresholds,\n74\t  export output).\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation\n79\t  steps — covered by the content outline above.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-945aaabf66655e09","agent_id":"a8655c8f05f6a5029","session_id":"14fa2f4a-f3d4-41e5-9c0e-f94b0cf4c56f","uuid":"167f9190-6bb3-48d6-a514-4537d0728224","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:18:44.602Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8adf36c08a82f201","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claud